WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.390
- Your show, "Who Do You Think You Are?"

00:00:01.390 --> 00:00:03.630
I was so excited to do it.

00:00:03.630 --> 00:00:06.190
Not only me but my mother was
very excited for me to do it.

00:00:06.190 --> 00:00:09.800
And when I did it, I just
had no idea coz my family,

00:00:09.800 --> 00:00:10.633
I mean all of us

00:00:10.633 --> 00:00:11.830
especially in America
we're all mutts, right?

00:00:11.830 --> 00:00:14.230
And there's so many different
layers to our background.

00:00:14.230 --> 00:00:16.130
And I just had no idea what direction

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.840
and it was the coolest thing ever

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.910
to find out about Isaiah R. Rose,

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:21.440
my great, great, great grandfather.

00:00:21.440 --> 00:00:22.840
It was like the coolest thing ever.

00:00:22.840 --> 00:00:26.150
What's the coolest thing you've
ever found out on that show?

00:00:26.150 --> 00:00:27.140
- The coolest thing?

00:00:27.140 --> 00:00:28.520
- Yeah, just anything that
sticks out on that show for you.

00:00:28.520 --> 00:00:30.670
- I have to say the thing that sticks out

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:32.180
since I started doing that show

00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:36.270
was how much I was learning about history

00:00:36.270 --> 00:00:38.520
that you don't learn in school.

00:00:38.520 --> 00:00:42.230
That there are these personal
stories and experiences

00:00:42.230 --> 00:00:44.820
that do not get taught at all.

00:00:44.820 --> 00:00:47.386
And just like the nuances of history

00:00:47.386 --> 00:00:49.160
that are really important

00:00:49.160 --> 00:00:51.670
to understand the context
for people's lives.

00:00:51.670 --> 00:00:52.503
So it's great.

00:00:52.503 --> 00:00:54.580
And I'm glad you brought
it up because we are,

00:00:54.580 --> 00:00:55.801
there's gonna be more.

00:00:55.801 --> 00:00:57.260
- What can we--
- On NBC.

00:00:57.260 --> 00:00:58.840
- Oh, on NBC?
- In July.

00:00:58.840 --> 00:00:59.673
- Oh that's amazing.

00:00:59.673 --> 00:01:01.306
- [Lisa] I know, I'm so happy.

00:01:01.306 --> 00:01:02.489
- What can we expect?

00:01:02.489 --> 00:01:04.130
Can you talk about anyone yet?

00:01:04.130 --> 00:01:06.080
- Yeah, I can tell you
who's gonna be in it.

00:01:06.080 --> 00:01:09.080
We have, we'll do six episodes.

00:01:09.080 --> 00:01:13.893
So we'll have Allison Janney, Zach Quinto.

00:01:15.980 --> 00:01:17.975
Oh, I knew that I would do this.

00:01:17.975 --> 00:01:18.950
(all laughing)

00:01:18.950 --> 00:01:20.200
Billy Porter.

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:21.230
- Oh wow.
- That's gonna be good.

00:01:21.230 --> 00:01:22.490
Nick Offerman.

00:01:22.490 --> 00:01:23.550
- [Kelly] I love him.

00:01:23.550 --> 00:01:26.320
- Yes, Zach Levi and Bradley Whitford.

00:01:26.320 --> 00:01:27.475
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:01:27.475 --> 00:01:28.308
- Yeah, yeah.

00:01:28.308 --> 00:01:29.290
They're great.

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:30.790
They're unbelievable stories.

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:33.460
- Yeah, it's just really
cool to dive into that

00:01:33.460 --> 00:01:36.221
and I never would've, and
I think just so you know,

00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:39.300
it's a cool experience for like,
I just grew up with my mom.

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:40.930
Like I didn't even grow up
with my brother or sister.

00:01:40.930 --> 00:01:42.210
Like I didn't grow up with any family,

00:01:42.210 --> 00:01:43.840
like aunts, uncles, grandparents, nothing.

00:01:43.840 --> 00:01:47.820
So to go into that show
and actually find family

00:01:47.820 --> 00:01:49.380
is really cool for a lot of people

00:01:49.380 --> 00:01:51.080
that didn't have that growing up.

00:01:51.080 --> 00:01:52.480
You feel attached to something.

00:01:52.480 --> 00:01:53.313
It's beautiful.

00:01:53.313 --> 00:01:54.400
- Yes, you're connected.

00:01:54.400 --> 00:01:55.640
You're connected to your roots

00:01:55.640 --> 00:01:59.020
and you're also connected to
the history of this place.

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.370
- And I've always felt
like a leaf, so no roots.

00:02:01.370 --> 00:02:02.543
So it was nice.

